  "description": "Shell commands and whether the MariaDB CLI guard must deny them. A command is denied only when it uses mariadb, mysql, mariadb-shell, mysqlsh or mariadb-dump for something an MCP tool covers. Every implementation of the guard (the bash hook for Claude Code and Codex, the Pi and OpenCode extensions, the Hermes plugin) is tested against this one list, plus one denied `mariadb-shell -- <object> <method>` call per entry of covered_shell_api, which maps each function called that way (<object>.<method> in snake_case, as the shell names it) to the MCP tool that wraps it; the denial names that tool.",
